---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quick start"
  description="Install Considered, initialize configuration, and run a check."
  current="/quick-start/"
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>Quick start</h1>
    <p>
      Considered ships as two binaries: the main CLI and the bundled
      <code>scc</code> provider. The CLI discovers providers by executable name,
      so both binaries must be on your <code>PATH</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Install with Homebrew</h2>
    <pre><code>brew install --cask quitepicky/tap/considered</code></pre>
    <p>The package installs both binaries together.</p>

    <h2>Windows</h2>
    <p>
      Download the Windows archive from
      <a href="https://github.com/quitepicky/considered/releases">GitHub Releases</a>,
      extract it, and add the directory containing both executables to your
      <code>PATH</code>. WinGet support is being prepared under
      <code>QuitePicky.Considered</code>; it will be available after the first
      community manifest submission is accepted.
    </p>

    <h2>Install from source</h2>
    <pre><code>git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/quitepicky/considered.git
cd considered
go build -o bin/considered ./cmd/considered
go build -o bin/considered-scc ./cmd/considered-scc</code></pre>

    <p>
      Put both binaries somewhere on your <code>PATH</code>, or add the local
      <code>bin/</code> directory while you are trying it out.
    </p>

    <h2>Initialize a repository</h2>
    <pre><code>considered init</code></pre>
    <p>
      This writes a starter <code>.considered.yaml</code> to the repository root.
      It fails if one already exists.
    </p>

    <h2>Run a check</h2>
    <pre><code>considered check</code></pre>
    <p>
      The text report separates failing violations from passing variances and
      near-boundary warnings.
    </p>

    <h2>Add a variance</h2>
    <pre><code>considered variance add \
  --subject src/parser/grammar.ts \
  --metric scc.code_lines \
  --kind architectural \
  --reason "Grammar definitions are intentionally centralized."</code></pre>

    <p>
      Considered captures the subject's current metric value as the approved
      boundary and writes the variance into the configuration.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
